{"id": 13, "ts": 1780608801.4971497, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s strong decision\u2011making and stress resilience, but the lack of any evidence of C\u2019s operational reliability is a serious gap for a long\u2011distance pilot role. As James confirmed, we have no record of C being dependable or consistent, and the only crew\u2011cooperation data point is that C \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d which raises concerns about cockpit harmony.\nIn contrast, we do have a concrete reliability indicator for Candidate\u202fB: he is described as \u201cvery conscientious,\u201d which directly signals a dependable work record. While B\u2019s notes also mention he can be \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative,\u201d those are behavioral traits we can address through training and team\u2011building, and they do not outweigh the proven reliability advantage.\nGiven the safety\u2011critical nature of this position, I am less convinced that C\u2019s strengths compensate for the unknown reliability and the clear crew\u2011cooperation weakness. I therefore shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fB**, pending further discussion of his teamwork profile."}
